# Use `default_if_empty` for String Fallbacks

When normalizing optional string inputs (CSV/env/config/request values), prefer
`string_utils.default_if_empty(value, default)` over inline empty checks.

```python
# BAD
reason = row[1] if len(row) > 1 else None
reason = reason.strip() if reason and reason.strip() else "no reason recorded"

# GOOD
reason = string_utils.default_if_empty(row[1], "no reason recorded")
```

Also replace ad-hoc forms like:
`value.strip() if value and value.strip() else fallback`

Keep explicit validation when a value is required and missing should raise, not
silently default.
